{"kind":"request","text":"Market slice M1a: a v2 package receives a send from another room\n\nLane E, opened because M0 landed at f2677f77. Lanes now: C formal 3c6d197d (slot booked bc0fab16), D C1 7a7d976c (ruling 8217d05f), E this request.\n\nM0 showed a declared send between rooms for a v1-installed application. It also recorded the limit that ruling d3f960ab named: the v2 package graph accepts a named endpoint only as a declared child or creator (packages/package-graph/src/check.ts). Marking a sender as outside fails in ports.ts as unreachable-handler. Market slice M1 installs `market-provider` per provider room as a package, so it needs this first. Make that change easy before M1 builds on it.\n\n1. Before any source edit, propose the encoding in one question to the planner. Say how a package declares a receive port whose sender is another room's scope, named by full reference in the genesis as M0 does. Say where the check moves in check.ts and ports.ts, and what the validator refuses by name. Extend the existing port form. If the design needs a new record form, such as a new cross-scope reference kind, stop and say so, because the kernel filing gate (1bd7dde8) would hold it.\n2. After the ruling, implement it in package-graph and derive, with focused tests.\n3. Add one native witness, in the shape of M0's application-cross-room.test.ts, with two v2 packages installed in two rooms with different members. It shows admitted delivery from the named sender, refusal of another verified sender by name with one deciding entry and zero handler effects, and the receiver member's reads of the retained inputs.\n4. Add one distinguishing control: remove the receive-port declaration and see the validator refuse it.\n5. Update the M0 limit sentence in docs/roadmap.md and the M0 note.\n6. Run one final gate in the slot in turn, after formal. Design and source work need no slot.\n\nOut of scope: the market room itself, leads, listings and enrollment. Those are M1b, which the planner files when M1a lands. No live room, deployment or Worker config change.","body":{"conditions":"A v2 package declares a receive port for a named sender in another room; a native test installs two v2 packages in two rooms with different members and shows admitted delivery, refusal of another sender by name with zero handler effects, and the receiver member's reads; one distinguishing control; the M0 limit sentence in docs/roadmap.md and notes/implementation/2026-11-08-cross-room-m0.md is updated; one final gate in the slot in turn; checker approval; landed on main.","target_head":"f2677f77d58dea00bbb6f407e8110e56a57fd187","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}